<title>USA: Precision Standard wins $63.4 mln deal.</title>
<headline>Precision Standard wins $63.4 mln deal.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Precision Standard Inc said on Thursday it had won a $63.4 million contract with the U.S. Air Force Space and Missile command to build sounding rocket launches.</p>
<p>Under the five-year contract, the company said it would suppply the launches for missile tests to be conducted by the military.</p>
